§ `Public Entertainments Act 1958 -- licensing`

§§ `First Schedule -- what is a public entertainment`

-- Para 2: "public entertainment" includes, in any place to which the public "or any class of the public" has access, "whether
-- gratuitously or otherwise": acrobatics and displays, circuses and animal exhibitions, amusement and computer games centres, film
-- shows, "any reproduction or transmission ... by any means other than telephony or radio telephony, of any music, song or speech",
-- prize machines, pin-tables, organised competitions at games of skill or chance, and arts entertainment (plays, exhibitions,
-- recitals, music, singing, dancing, and their live-streamed transmission).
-- Para 3: it does NOT include (a) official foreign-government gatherings; (b) Government or local-authority entertainment; (c)
-- religious ceremonies in consecrated premises "where any discourse, sermon, lecture, talk or address ... is ONLY given by persons who
-- are citizens or permanent residents of Singapore"; (d) members-only meetings of public companies, chambers of commerce, unions,
-- platform work associations, political associations or societies; (e) statutory boards; (f) "any lecture, talk, address, debate or
-- discussion".
DECLARE Event HAS
    `the public has access` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a listed form of entertainment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a lecture, talk or debate only` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is run by the Government or a statutory board` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a religious service in consecrated premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a foreign preacher speaks` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a members-only meeting of a company, union or society` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the event` IS AN Event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the event is a public entertainment` IF
        `the event`'s `the public has access`
    AND `the event`'s `is a listed form of entertainment`
    AND (NOT `the event`'s `is a lecture, talk or debate only`)
    AND (NOT `the event`'s `is run by the Government or a statutory board`)
    AND (NOT (`the event`'s `is a religious service in consecrated premises` AND (NOT `the event`'s `a foreign preacher speaks`)))
    AND (NOT `the event`'s `is a members-only meeting of a company, union or society`)

§§ `4, 28 -- the licence and the offences`

-- s 4: a public entertainment must not be provided except in an approved place and under a licence.
-- s 28(1): providing or assisting in providing one (a) without a licence or (b) while suspended -- up to $20,000; (c) in breach of a
-- condition or (d) otherwise in contravention -- up to $10,000. (2): no one provides or assists "merely by reason of the person having
-- taken part" -- performers are not liable.
-- (3): false or misleading information, known, negligent ("ought reasonably to know") or reckless -- up to $5,000.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the organiser`
    `the venue operator assisting`
    `a performer`
    `an audience member`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role can commit the unlicensed-entertainment offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `the organiser` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the venue operator assisting` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Breach IS ONE OF
    `no licence`
    `licence suspended`
    `breach of a licence condition`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the breach`
    WHEN `breach of a licence condition` THEN 10000
    OTHERWISE 20000

§§ `32 -- onus of proof`

-- s 32: "the onus of proving that the public or any class of the public did NOT have access to any public entertainment lies on the
-- person alleging the fact" -- in practice, the defendant who says the event was private.
GIVEN `the defendant proved no public access` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the event is treated as having public access` IF
    NOT `the defendant proved no public access`
